[b]Single player only. Build 42.[/b]

Adds a Starting Gear section to the clothing page of character creation. Pick what goes on your belt, holster, back and modded sling slots, what you hold in each hand, and what goes in every bag you wear. Slots and items come from the same tables the hotbar uses, so modded clothing and items show up with no setup.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*]Make a character as usual. Starting Gear is under the clothing choices.
[*]Bags: one chooser per place a bag can be worn, including ones mods add.
[*]Attached items: a slot appears for each belt, holster or sling you wear. Only items that fit are listed.
[*]Edit contents... on a bag opens the item list with category and name filters, any quantity, and the bag's weight against its capacity.
[*]Firearm attachments: scopes, lights, lasers, slings and so on for any gun you picked, each showing what it changes. No screwdriver needed.
[*]A tick box, on by default, starts guns and magazines fully loaded.
[*]Gear is saved with the vanilla Save build presets, and your last picks are remembered.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Only affects a new character made on the creation screen.
[*]Also fixes a vanilla bug where a saved build lost everything after a modded item with a namespaced body location (like Alice's Weapon Sling).
[*]Single player only.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]The first open reads the whole item list, which takes a few seconds on a big mod list.
[*]Parts go on every copy of that gun type. Parts and hand items don't show on the preview.
[*]If the preview can't draw your gear it falls back to the normal one. You still get the gear.
[*]Hand items are weapons only, and overweight bags aren't blocked.
[/list]

Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/maxcwolf/pz-mods/tree/main/choose-starting-gear]GitHub[/url]
